earc_route.c is derived from Glasshouse's native-route.c, and build.py from its
build-target.py (https://github.com/rorygallagher2024/glasshouse,
native/dts-forwarding, GPL-2.0-only). Glasshouse designed and qualified the
route: the producer lease, watchdog, DTS-HD mode, restore and hand-back paths
are its work. This port replaces Glasshouse's exact-image addresses with
earc_decode.h, which derives them from LG's code at load time, and adds the
loader and the host test.

The module contains no LG code. It calls LG's kernel functions at run time and
reads their machine code to find the data they use. Kernel images, kallsyms
captures and stock modules from LG TVs are LG's files: they stay outside this
repository and are only read by the build and the tests.

